Local patches:
- patches/0001-pluggable-main-window-finder.patch — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py gets
  set_main_window_finder(fn) and _find_main_window(), used at the three
  _find_nuke_main_window() call sites, so a non-Nuke host (Natron) can plug
  in its own main-window lookup; _find_nuke_main_window itself and Nuke's
  behaviour are unchanged.
- patches/0002-host-row-metrics.patch — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py gets
  set_row_metrics(row_height, visible_rows), used by TabTabTabWidget in
  place of the hardcoded "twice the font height" row and 18 visible rows,
  so a host can size the popup to its own row height; defaults are
  unchanged, so Nuke's sizing is untouched. Also extracts the popup's
  cursor-relative placement into _popup_position(), which now flips the
  list above the search box instead of pushing the whole popup up the
  screen when it doesn't fit below the cursor.
- tests/test_host_hooks.py is a new test file, added by Natron (not from
  upstream), covering set_main_window_finder(), _find_main_window(),
  set_row_metrics(), _row_height(), _visible_rows() and _popup_position().
